  "headline": "Stew Trades Two Running Backs for Yesterday’s Superstar",
  "publicationDraft": "Stew gambled on A.J. Green rediscovering his Pro Bowl form, despite a lost 2019 season and an ugly three-catch, 13-target outing the week before the deal. Evans picked up Ronald Jones and Nyheim Hines, two backs with uncertain workloads but genuine opportunity. Jones went on to rush for 978 yards, while Green was dropped, reacquired for free and dropped again. His lone 2.90-point start came after reacquisition, not during the original trade ownership spell. Hines supplied 9.50 observed starter points before Evans cut him, while Jones supplied 82.40. Jones missed Weeks 15–16 with injury/COVID complications. Stew traded for the name; Evans traded for the opportunity. Neither managed every subsequent lineup perfectly.",
